---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Jędrzej Szymula — Content & SEO Specialist"
  description="Jędrzej Szymula — content and SEO specialist making brands findable in Google, in AI answers, and across markets from Warsaw to the U.S."
  path="/home-globe.html"
  active="home"
  homeHref="home-globe.html"
  robots="noindex"
  bodyClass="globe-home"
>

  <section class="g-hero" aria-labelledby="g-headword">
    <article class="g-entry" id="g-entry" aria-live="polite">
      <p class="g-kicker">Entry № 001 · <em>noun</em></p>
      <h2 class="g-headword" id="g-headword">Jędrzej Szymula</h2>
      <p class="g-pron">/ˈjɛn.dʐɛj ʂɨˈmu.la/</p>
      <ol class="g-senses">
        <li>A content &amp; SEO specialist who makes brands findable — in Google, in AI answers, and across markets from Warsaw to the U.S.</li>
        <li><span class="g-label">informal</span> The person you call when the blog has to grow 2× and the AI has to quote you.</li>
      </ol>
      <dl class="g-stats">
        <div><dt>2×</dt><dd>Blog growth YoY</dd></div>
        <div><dt>1,000+</dt><dd>TOP 3 keywords</dd></div>
        <div><dt>40</dt><dd>AI citations</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <div class="g-actions">
        <a href="work.html" class="btn">See the work</a>
        <a href="mailto:j.szymula.seo@gmail.com" class="btn btn-ghost">Work with me</a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Topic panels shown in the entry box when a globe tag is hovered/tapped.
         Edit freely: kicker, headword, expansion, text, two buttons. -->
    <div class="g-topics" hidden>
      <div data-topic="SEO">
        <p class="g-kicker">Entry № 002 · <em>abbr.</em></p>
        <h2 class="g-headword">SEO</h2>
        <p class="g-pron">Search Engine Optimization</p>
        <p class="g-intro">Making pages rank in Google and Bing: technical foundations, content mapped to real search intent, and authority that compounds. For winiety-online.pl that meant 1,000+ keywords in TOP 3 and over $125K in content-driven sales.</p>
        <div class="g-actions">
          <a href="knowledge.html#seo" class="btn">Learn more</a>
          <a href="mailto:j.szymula.seo@gmail.com?subject=SEO%20project" class="btn btn-ghost">Hire me</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div data-topic="AEO">
        <p class="g-kicker">Entry № 003 · <em>abbr.</em></p>
        <h2 class="g-headword">AEO</h2>
        <p class="g-pron">Answer Engine Optimization</p>
        <p class="g-intro">Writing content so it becomes the answer — featured snippets, “People also ask”, voice and AI answer boxes. Clear questions, extractable answers, structured data. Built at scale for Flobotics: 30+ glossary terms and 40+ FAQ pieces.</p>
        <div class="g-actions">
          <a href="knowledge.html#aeo" class="btn">Learn more</a>
          <a href="mailto:j.szymula.seo@gmail.com?subject=AEO%20consultation" class="btn btn-ghost">Consult me</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div data-topic="GEO">
        <p class="g-kicker">Entry № 004 · <em>abbr.</em></p>
        <h2 class="g-headword">GEO</h2>
        <p class="g-pron">Generative Engine Optimization</p>
        <p class="g-intro">Getting a brand cited by ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity and Google AI Overviews — through consistent mentions across the web, JSON-LD and llms.txt. For Flobotics: 40 AI citations and AI Overviews in 3 months.</p>
        <div class="g-actions">
          <a href="knowledge.html#geo" class="btn">Learn more</a>
          <a href="mailto:j.szymula.seo@gmail.com?subject=GEO%20project" class="btn btn-ghost">Hire me</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div data-topic="AI">
        <p class="g-kicker">Entry № 005 · <em>noun</em></p>
        <h2 class="g-headword">AI</h2>
        <p class="g-pron">AI-assisted content operations</p>
        <p class="g-intro">Using AI for research, briefs, fact-checking and site builds — with a human editor accountable for every claim. Two site migrations, the latest to a custom Astro site built with AI assistance.</p>
        <div class="g-actions">
          <a href="work.html#flobotics" class="btn">Learn more</a>
          <a href="mailto:j.szymula.seo@gmail.com?subject=AI%20content%20consultation" class="btn btn-ghost">Consult me</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div data-topic="B2B">
        <p class="g-kicker">Entry № 006 · <em>adj.</em></p>
        <h2 class="g-headword">B2B</h2>
        <p class="g-pron">Business-to-business content</p>
        <p class="g-intro">Content for long sales cycles and expert buyers: case studies, market reports and founder-led LinkedIn. Flagship: the State of RCM Automation 2026 report — 61 sources, 4 expert voices, 3 fact-check passes.</p>
        <div class="g-actions">
          <a href="work.html#flobotics" class="btn">See the report</a>
          <a href="mailto:j.szymula.seo@gmail.com?subject=B2B%20content" class="btn btn-ghost">Hire me</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <a href="#g-more" class="g-scroll">Scroll ↓</a>
  </section>

  <div class="g-after" id="g-more">

    <div class="section-label">See also</div>

    <article class="entry">
      <div class="entry-header">
        <span class="entry-word">Case Studies</span>
      </div>
      <p class="entry-definition">
        Documented accounts of content and SEO work — the starting conditions, what was done, and what changed.
      </p>
      <div class="index-grid index-grid--spaced">
        <a href="work.html#flobotics" class="index-item">
          <span class="index-item-word">Flobotics</span>
          <span class="index-item-desc">100K+ reached · Healthcare RCM · 2025–now</span>
        </a>
        <a href="work.html#autopay" class="index-item">
          <span class="index-item-word">mobility.autopay.eu</span>
          <span class="index-item-desc">4.89M impressions · Fintech · 2024–26</span>
        </a>
        <a href="work.html#milo-solutions" class="index-item">
          <span class="index-item-word">Milo Solutions</span>
          <span class="index-item-desc">1,800+ daily visits in 3 months · IT · 2024</span>
        </a>
        <a href="work.html#winiety-online" class="index-item">
          <span class="index-item-word">winiety-online.pl</span>
          <span class="index-item-desc">1,000+ TOP 3 keywords · E-commerce · 2024</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <a href="work.html" class="btn btn-ghost">Read full case studies →</a>
    </article>

    <article class="entry">
      <div class="entry-header">
        <span class="entry-word">SEO · AEO · GEO</span>
      </div>
      <p class="entry-definition">
        Ranking in search results, being the extracted answer, and being the brand an AI model reaches for.
        Three overlapping disciplines, explained in plain language.
      </p>
      <a href="knowledge.html" class="btn btn-ghost">Open the Knowledge entries →</a>
    </article>

    <article class="entry">
      <div class="entry-header">
        <span class="entry-word">Resources</span>
      </div>
      <p class="entry-definition">
        Practical checklists and guides distilled from real client work. Launching soon.
      </p>
      <a href="shop.html" class="btn btn-ghost">See what's coming →</a>
    </article>

  </div>

  <Fragment slot="before">
  <!-- Decorative rotating globe: big close-up, its upper-right limb sits in the
       bottom-left quarter of the first screen and fades out at the bottom. -->
  <canvas id="globe" class="globe-canvas" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
  <!-- Glitchy pop-up tags pinned to points on the globe (filled by globe.js) -->
  <div id="globe-tags" class="globe-tags" aria-label="Topics — hover or tap one to read about it"></div>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="scripts">
  <!-- Land shapes for the globe (free CDN, no build step). If they fail to load,
       globe.js falls back to a plain dotted sphere. -->
  <script is:inline src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/d3-array@3.2.4/dist/d3-array.min.js"></script>
  <script is:inline src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/d3-geo@3.1.1/dist/d3-geo.min.js"></script>
  <script is:inline src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/topojson-client@3.1.0/dist/topojson-client.min.js"></script>
  <script is:inline src="globe.js"></script>
  </Fragment>
</Base>
